Dockerfile – Shell Script Execution
1)create the shell script:
#!/bin/bash
echo "The current system date and time is: $(date)"
2) Create the Dockerfile:
# Use a lightweight Linux base
FROM alpine:latest
# Install bash (Alpine uses 'sh' by default)
RUN apk add --no-cache bash
# Set the working directory
WORKDIR /app
# Copy the script into the container
COPY script.sh .
# Make the script executable
RUN chmod +x script.sh
# Run the script when the container starts
CMD ["./script.sh"]
3)Build the image:     docker build -t my-shell-app .
4) Run the container:  docker run my-shell-app


Shared Volume Between Containers
1)Create the Shared Volume:     docker volume create shared_data
2)Start the First Container:    docker run --name con1 -v shared_data:/common alpine sh -c "echo 'Shared data from Container A' > /common/hello.txt"
3)Start the Second Container:   docker run --name reader-container -v shared_data:/common alpine cat /common/hello.txt

